WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.280
Every metabolic pathway falls into one of two camps, and keeping them straight will

2
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.760
carry you through the whole course.

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.340
Catabolic pathways break large molecules down.

4
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.680
They combust carbon fuels like carbohydrates and fats to carbon dioxide and water,

5
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.340
and they capture the released energy as ATP or as ion gradients.

6
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.100
Anabolic pathways run the other direction.

7
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.180
They take simple precursors and spend energy and reducing power to build complex

8
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.580
biomolecules. So catabolism releases energy by tearing down.

9
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.360
Anabolism consumes energy to assemble.

10
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.000
The cell is constantly running both at once, with the products of one feeding the

11
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.000
other.

12
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:48.450
A reaction that won't go on its own can be forced uphill if we link it to one that

13
00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.450
wants to go downhill.

14
00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:56.350
On the left, A to B plus C has a positive delta G of plus 21, so alone it stalls.

15
00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:01.690
On the right, we couple it to a strongly favorable reaction with a delta G of minus

16
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:08.910
34. Add them, and the net delta G is minus 13, comfortably negative, so the combined

17
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:13.090
pathway proceeds. This is the central trick of metabolism.

18
00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:18.410
Individual steps must be specific, but only the pathway as a whole has to be

19
00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.850
thermodynamically favorable.

20
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.850
Coupling is how the cell pays for the reactions it needs.

21
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:29.503
ATP hydrolysis is exergonic and four distinct effects explain why.

22
00:01:30.603 --> 00:01:31.903
First, charge repulsion drops.

23
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:37.043
The triphosphate tail carries several closely packed negative charges and cutting it

24
00:01:37.043 --> 00:01:38.623
apart relieves that strain.

25
00:01:39.503 --> 00:01:44.143
Second, resonance stabilization increases because inorganic phosphate has more

26
00:01:44.143 --> 00:01:47.963
equivalent resonance forms than the phosphate locked inside ATP.

27
00:01:48.743 --> 00:01:52.223
Third, entropy rises since one molecule becomes two.

28
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:56.583
Fourth, the products are better stabilized by water through hydration than the

29
00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.283
reactant was. No single factor dominates.

30
00:01:59.723 --> 00:02:01.563
Together, they make hydrolysis favorable.

31
00:02:02.303 --> 00:02:07.623
Crucially, ATP is thermodynamically unstable but kinetically stable, so it doesn't

32
00:02:07.623 --> 00:02:09.863
waste itself until an enzyme calls on it.

33
00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:13.093
Here's the payoff of coupling, made quantitative.

34
00:02:13.653 --> 00:02:18.293
An unfavorable reaction sitting alone has an equilibrium constant of about one-one

35
00:02:18.293 --> 00:02:20.813
-thousandth, so almost no product forms.

36
00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:24.333
Now couple that same reaction to ATP hydrolysis.

37
00:02:24.993 --> 00:02:29.893
The favorable energy of hydrolysis adds in, the combined equilibrium constant jumps

38
00:02:29.893 --> 00:02:33.373
to roughly 267, and product now dominates.

39
00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:38.413
That's a shift of about 10 to the fifth, a hundred-thousand-fold change in where

40
00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:39.433
the reaction settles.

41
00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:44.413
This single idea is why ATP is the cell's universal coupling agent.

42
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:49.193
Spending one phosphoanhydride bond can drag an otherwise hopeless reaction all the

43
00:02:49.193 --> 00:02:50.193
way to completion.

44
00:02:50.717 --> 00:02:55.437
The cell monitors its own energy state with a number called the energy charge, and

45
00:02:55.437 --> 00:02:57.957
it works like a fuel gauge running from zero to one.

46
00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:03.917
The formula weights ATP fully and ADP half, then divides by the total adenylate

47
00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:08.957
pool, so a cell loaded with ATP reads near the top and a depleted cell reads low.

48
00:03:09.617 --> 00:03:11.417
This single value governs flux.

49
00:03:11.977 --> 00:03:16.717
When the charge is high, the cell throttles down catabolic ATP-generating pathways

50
00:03:16.717 --> 00:03:19.957
and turns up anabolic ATP-spending ones.

51
00:03:20.257 --> 00:03:22.557
When the charge falls, it does the reverse.

52
00:03:23.417 --> 00:03:27.737
Energy charge is the master signal balancing energy production against energy

53
00:03:27.737 --> 00:03:28.257
consumption.
